{"schema": "workere-benchmark-suite/v1", "protocol": "workere-historical-relations/v1", "config": {"seed": 42, "active_dataset": "causal_timebank", "datasets": {"causal_timebank": {"name": "CausalTimeBank-standard-eci", "repo_id": "Nofing/CausalTimeBank-standard-eci-workere", "split": "train", "text_field": "text", "ann_field": "annots", "max_examples": 0, "kfold": {"enabled": true, "n_folds": 10}, "constrain_to_pair_list": false}}, "data": {"shuffle_docs": true, "shuffle_pair_list": true, "reshuffle_per_resample": true, "binary_undirected": false, "vote_to_binary": false, "binary_default": "norel", "novote_norel": true, "labels": ["causes", "causedby", "norel"]}, "experiment": {"resampling": {"enabled": true, "n_runs": 7, "tie_breaking": "norel", "distinct_fewshots": true}}}, "documents": [{"id": "PRI19980303.2000.2550", "idx": 38, "text": "Tomorrow the board of supervisors of Loudon county , Virginia , will <ei2 vote> on whether a school now <ei4 located> in Mount Vernon can <ei5 relocate> to their county . In some respects , that 's typical county business , but tomorrow 's <ei7 vote> has international implications . The board will <ei8 decide> whether the Islamic Saudi Academy , <ei9 funded> by the government of Saudi Arabia , can <ei10 move> to Ashburn village , Virginia . But local residents have not exactly <ei11 laid> out the red carpet for their would be neighbors . The World 's Nancy Marshalll has our story . Inside the Islamic Saudi academy in Mount Vernon , Virginia , many of the girls wear head scarves and some of the neatly dressed children are in uniforms . The instruction is in English for most classes , in Arabic for language and religious studies . The school says it teaches the children to be good Muslims and good students . They 're learning a civics lesson from the residents of Loudon county . The Islamic Saudi Academy has twelve hundred mostly American students but would <ei12 take> thirty-five hundred if it <ei13 had> the room . The academy <ei14 bought> a hundred acres in Loudon county , Virginia , and <ei15 asked> for permission to <ei16 build> a fifty million dollar campus . In the nearby suburban housing tracts , someone <ei17 dropped> off leaflets <ei18 warning> the school could <ei19 bring> thousands of Middle Eastern strangers and terrorists . Some residents of the mostly white , mostly middle class area <ei20 became> alarmed . James Zogby of the Arab American Institute <ei21 says> it 's a familiar story . There is , a - at a very deep level in our culture , um I <ei22 think> , a sense of , of ignorance about Islam , a fear about who Muslims are and what they 're doing . Many local residents <ei23 denounced> the bigotry , but opposition to the school then <ei24 shifted> . Now critics of the academy are <ei26 targeting> its owner , the Saudi government . Pastor James Allmen of the fellowship church and school in Ashburn has <ei27 led> the anti-Saudi <ei28 campaign> . James Allmen <ei29 says> he <ei30 has> no problem with a privately funded academy , but he <ei31 has> a big problem with a Saudi funded school . The Saudi Arabian government has an atrocious record on human rights and is known to be one of the worst offending countries when it comes to religious persecution . That 's correct . And that is a condition of the application , then . At a public <ei32 hearing> on the Islamic Saudi Academy 's application , the <ei33 split> in county opinion was obvious , supporters of the academy , including Ann Robinson , <ei34 said> the Saudis were just <ei35 providing> a service and it was <ei36 unfair> to <ei37 penalize> children . We do not <ei38 further> the purpose of human rights in the world by <ei39 violating> the human rights under our own constitution . But opponents <ei40 said> the school might be a target for terrorist <ei41 attacks> , <ei42 complained> about its tax exempt status , and <ei43 wondered> why the Saudis are not <ei44 compelled> to <ei45 allow> Christians to <ei46 worship> in their country . Virginia Welch <ei47 delivered> this message to the county board of supervisors . I <ei48 urge> you to <ei49 do> the right thing and <ei50 send> a message to the Saudis that the citizens of Loudon county <ei51 embrace> religious and human freedom . Loudon county officials <ei52 say> they 'll <ei53 rule> on the application based only on land use issues and <ei54 ignore> all the other objections . What 's really behind those objections , some <ei55 say> , is Loudon county 's <ei56 collision> with a new reality in America that the country is <ei57 changing> religiously as surely as it is racially and ethnically . <ei58 According> to the Arab American institute , Islam will one day be the second largest religion in the country . For an indication of the problems that could face Muslims as they integrate into American life , one need look no farther than Loudon county , Virginia . For The World , I 'm Nancy Marshalll .", "gold": [], "lang": "eng", "mentions": ["ei2", "ei4", "ei5", "ei7", "ei8", "ei9", "ei10", "ei11", "ei12", "ei13", "ei14", "ei15", "ei16", "ei17", "ei18", "ei19", "ei20", "ei21", "ei22", "ei23", "ei24", "ei26", "ei27", "ei28", "ei29", "ei30", "ei31", "ei32", "ei33", "ei34", "ei35", "ei36", "ei37", "ei38", "ei39", "ei40", "ei41", "ei42", "ei43", "ei44", "ei45", "ei46", "ei47", "ei48", "ei49", "ei50", "ei51", "ei52", "ei53", "ei54", "ei55", "ei56", "ei57", "ei58"], "surfaces": {"ei2": "vote", "ei4": "located", "ei5": "relocate", "ei7": "vote", "ei8": "decide", "ei9": "funded", "ei10": "move", "ei11": "laid", "ei12": "take", "ei13": "had", "ei14": "bought", "ei15": "asked", "ei16": "build", "ei17": "dropped", "ei18": "warning", "ei19": "bring", "ei20": "became", "ei21": "says", "ei22": "think", "ei23": "denounced", "ei24": "shifted", "ei26": "targeting", "ei27": "led", "ei28": "campaign", "ei29": "says", "ei30": "has", "ei31": "has", "ei32": "hearing", "ei33": "split", "ei34": "said", "ei35": "providing", "ei36": "unfair", "ei37": "penalize", "ei38